-The neural network acts only on the output of the graph algorithm. Whereas Ralphi\cite{battistella2025ralphi} and NeurHap\cite{xue2022neurhap} learn haplotype assembly itself and must scale to whole chromosomes, \toolname confines learning to windows around high-entropy variants; inference adds one to two minutes per genome, and the 687,358 parameters are compiled into the binary. The closest precedent is the likelihood-based pruning of \hapcut\cite{edge2017hapcut2}, which withholds variants whose posterior under the phasing model falls below a threshold. The network instead reads the structure of the evidence across a window (vote totals, entropy, sequence context, graph topology and the concordance of neighbours), where correlated errors from mis-mapped reads and paralogues should leave a trace; comparisons with \hapcut pruning and with a fixed entropy threshold, at matched numbers of withheld variants, are still needed to establish what it adds over simpler rules. Because the correction only withholds phase, part of its gain follows by construction, and what matters is what it withholds and at what price. At 60$\times$ the network withdrew phase from about 60,000 SNVs while switch errors fell from 743 to 496, block N50 fell by less than 2\% and the phased fraction stayed within one percentage point of \whatshap; at 10$\times$ the price was higher, with 14\% of the unphased SNVs heterozygous in the benchmark and N50 falling from 0.92 to 0.84~Mb. The assembly analysis qualifies how the rest should be read. Most removed calls were not refuted by the truth set but lay outside its reach: 88\% fell outside the regions in which the T2T-HG002 assembly aligns one-to-one to GRCh38, concentrated in pericentromeric satellites, against 7\% of SNVs phased before correction, and about half of those inside lacked an assembly variant record at the same coordinate. Their phase there cannot be verified with this truth set, and would otherwise pass unqualified to haplotagged reads and the somatic callers that consume them\cite{zheng2026clairs,chen2025clairsto,keskus2025severus}. The two tools also left largely different SNVs unphased, \whatshap mostly at low depth and \toolname at normal or excess depth, and each set was enriched up to tenfold in genomic intervals containing switch disagreements of the other tool; this is regional co-location, not evidence that each withheld site would have been misphased. Two further observations bear on how such corrections should be judged. Margin made fewer switch errors than \toolname at 10$\times$, which coincided with blocks three times shorter; a switch-error count means little without the contiguity that accompanies it. And the network, trained only on nanopore reads, removed 19--28\% of the switch errors of \toolname on PacBio HiFi data, against 31--33\% on nanopore data, at a cost of 1--2\% of block N50, which suggests that the error signatures it has learned are not specific to one platform, at least within HG002.
-
-Several limitations remain. The evaluation rests on one individual, HG002, and the network was trained on its nanopore data: its labels came from the evaluation benchmark and its windows from the same down-sampling replicates at 10--20$\times$, and only chr17, chr21 and chr22 were withheld from training, whereas the switch error rates reported here are genome-wide (Methods). The network's gains therefore require confirmation on held-out chromosomes, on an independent individual and benchmark with frozen weights and thresholds, and above 20$\times$, and a comparison with simpler withholding rules at matched numbers of withheld variants\todo{The training-label code matches truth records by position only, without REF/ALT, accepts unphased truth genotypes and compares phase within query phase sets alone (\texttt{prepare\_gnn\_data\_10.py}:343, 440). Audit the training records for allele mismatches, unphased truth and truth-block crossings; if any are found, correct the labels and retrain}. Two design choices bound the cost of a miscalibrated model, although neither is evidence of generalization: its features are generic (no sequence embeddings or sample-specific statistics), and a model restricted to withholding phase can cost contiguity but cannot create haplotypes. The HiFi evaluation used the same individual, a single replicate per coverage and, apparently, one call set for every coverage; it establishes transfer across platforms but not across individuals; duplex chemistries and non-human genomes are untested, values at 30--60$\times$ come from a single replicate, and Margin, Ralphi and GCphase were compared only at 10--20$\times$. For indels, SVs and 5mC sites we report how many were phased, not whether they were phased correctly; their phased fraction is bounded by the upstream callers, and the network's corrections to SV and 5mC phase are unsupervised, because the truth set labels only small variants. 5mC co-phasing requires modification-aware base calling, whose accuracy varies between callers and chemistries\cite{sigurpalsdottir2024methylation}, and was assessed only on the autosomes of a male lymphoblastoid cell line, whereas allele-specific methylation differs between tissues and random X inactivation makes X-linked methylation inconsistent between cells of female samples\cite{fu2024methphaser}; and among methylation-aware phasers\cite{fu2024methphaser,chen2025hapbridge,pfennig2026longhap} only MethPhaser was compared, which left the haplotypes it was given unchanged in our hands. Finally, \toolname assumes a diploid genome with balanced allele fractions, which excludes aneuploid tumour genomes and polyploid organisms.
-
-Trio assembly\cite{cheng2021hifiasm,rautiainen2023verkko}, Hi-C\cite{selvaraj2013hic} and Strand-seq\cite{porubsky2021fully} reach chromosome scale but need extra samples or libraries, and imputation\cite{sun2025advances,ebler2022pangenie} depends on reference panels that remain sparse for structural variation and for many populations; \toolname needs one sample and one library, and per-variant phasing evidence makes its haplotypes a natural input to hybrid read-plus-panel strategies\cite{liao2023pangenome,hofmeister2023shapeit5}. As a drop-in replacement in pipelines already built on \longphase\cite{zheng2022clair3,zheng2026clairs,keskus2025severus,ont2025wfhuman}, \toolname adds these annotations without interface changes, and they have concrete uses. A compound-heterozygous diagnosis rests on a single \textit{trans} call between two variants in one gene\cite{eisfeldt2025clinical,negi2025napu}; the entropy and vote totals of those two variants can flag the calls that warrant a confirmatory assay. Allele-specific methylation analyses typically treat every haplotagged read alike, whereas weighting reads by the phasing evidence of the variants that tagged them would keep imprinting and \textit{cis}-regulatory signals\cite{akbari2023parentoforigin} from being diluted by thinly supported blocks. Haplotype-aware somatic callers\cite{zheng2026clairs,keskus2025severus} likewise accept inherited phase without qualification and could discount the loci at which switch errors concentrate. Realizing these uses will require a calibrated per-variant confidence and downstream tools that read it, much as they came to read genotype quality.
+As a drop-in replacement in pipelines built on \longphase\cite{zheng2022clair3,zheng2026clairs,keskus2025severus,ont2025wfhuman}, \toolname adds per-variant phasing evidence without interface changes. The most direct use is in haplotype-aware somatic calling\cite{zheng2026clairs,keskus2025severus}, which accepts inherited phase without qualification: withholding phase at the loci where switch errors concentrate should keep spurious germline phase out of haplotagged tumour reads. Testing that, by varying only the germline phaser upstream of a fixed somatic caller, and providing a calibrated per-variant confidence that downstream tools can read, as they read genotype quality, are the next steps.
